Message Trace

Message Trace was used to investigate email delivery.
Example:
Sarah Williams
      ↓
Bob John

I used:
Exchange Admin Center → Mail flow → Message trace

Message Trace showed:
Received
   ↓
Processed
   ↓
Delivered

The message details confirmed delivery to the recipient’s mailbox.

Why Message Trace Matters

If a user reports:

“I sent an email but the recipient didn’t receive it.”

an administrator shouldn’t immediately assume the message was lost.

Message Trace can help determine whether Exchange:

* received the message
* processed it
* delivered it
* encountered a failure

This provides evidence before troubleshooting further.
